    "answer": "to: become-loose/slacken-(e.g.-rope) | become-less-tense/relax/let-one's-guard-down | slacken-(e.g.-coldness,-supervision)/become-lax | to-become-softer-(e.g.-ground,-facial-expression)/(of-ice)-to-partially-melt | decrease-(e.g.-speed) | (of-a-market-price)-to-go-down-slightly",
    "mnemonic": "Because the hiragana ends with an <ja>う</ja> sound, you know this word is a verb. The kanji itself means <kanji>loose</kanji>, so the verb version is <vocabulary>to loosen</vocabulary>. This is when something loosens on its own, and not via your actions. You know this because a cow is loosening things, <reading>moo</reading> (<ja>む</ja>)...",
